 "kind": "cup",
 "lineage_note": "Europe's top club cup. 1955-56 to 1991-92 = European Champion Clubs' Cup (European Cup); 1992-93 on = UEFA Champions League (same competition, same trophy, same records). Top scorer uses UEFA's convention: goals in the main competition only (from 1992-93 the group/league phase to the final; qualifying and play-off rounds excluded; before 1992 every round counts). Top scorer values are kept only where two independent sources agree (Wikipedia's season list, RSSSF, UEFA's own statistics database); 1964-65 has three different answers (José Torres 11 / Torres and Eusébio 9 / Torres and Eusébio 6), so the continuous run starts 1965-66. Top assister = UEFA's official assist count (main competition only), which UEFA's statistics database holds without a break from 2001-02; nothing official exists before that. Penalty-shoot-out finals were all 1-1/0-0/3-3 after extra time. 1973-74 needed a replay. Club names are the common English names used by UEFA/Wikipedia lists (e.g. Inter Milan, Bayern Munich, Red Star Belgrade).",
